    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-merge-queue-author-side/folio-assistant/folio-assistant.jsonld#directory/memory",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/ns#Subgraph",
      "name": "memory",
      "path": "memory/",
      "contentSource": {
        "kind": "directory",
        "declaredIn": "default"
      },
      "holdsGraph": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#graphKind/memory",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#graphKind/waiver"
      ],
      "description": "Agent memory — durable facts an agent carries between sessions, one `\"$schema\": \"folio-memory/v1\"` node each, assembled into `.claude/agent-memory/<agent>/MEMORY.md`. `context` by the axis bean `mhh9` settled: read during a process, never written by one; it changes when a human directs an authoring agent. It sat in `skills/memory/` until 2026-09-20 — inside the `cat-harness` directory, which is `content` — so the CONTAINING kind and the contents were on opposite layers, and a nested declaration is the defect #263 names. Moving it was held back from the classification change on purpose (#395's rule, and bean `auap`'s precedent: a relocation is its own change) and is bean `07xs`. SCOPE IS `repository`, like `beans/`: these are facts about this REPOSITORY carried by the agents working in it, and `.claude/agents/` — the consumers — sit at the repository root too.",
      "readmePath": "memory/README.md",
      "fileCount": 47,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-merge-queue-author-side/folio-assistant/folio-assistant.jsonld#directory/memory",
      "alternateOf": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/folio-assistant/folio-assistant.jsonld#directory/memory"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-merge-queue-author-side/folio-assistant/folio-assistant.jsonld#directory/interaction",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/ns#Subgraph",
      "name": "interaction",
      "path": "interaction/",
      "contentSource": {
        "kind": "directory",
        "declaredIn": "default"
      },
      "holdsGraph": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#graphKind/interaction"
      ],
      "description": "How a PERSON wants to be asked — committed, read at session start by every agent. `context` by the same test as agent memory: read during a process, never written by one, changed when a person states a preference. It sat in `.harness/`, undeclared, until 2026-09-20, which this repository's own dot-prefix guard forbids: a dot-prefixed directory is absent from a plain `ls`, from most file browsers and from a forge's web tree, and the file read at the start of every session was in the one place the conventions reject. The path is also `harness.config.json`'s `interaction` key, which defaults here — the declaration and the config now name the same place instead of one of them being a literal nobody checks. SCOPE IS `repository`, and omitting it was a live defect for an hour on 2026-09-20: without it the path resolves against the INSTANCE, so a consumer looked in `cat-harness/` while the content sat at the repository root — and `harness:dirs` then created the empty instance-level directory to satisfy the declaration, turning declared-but-absent into declared-and-empty, which is the `dh4f` false pass wearing a tidier face. Repository, not instance, for the same reason `beans/` and `todos/` are: these are read by every agent working in this repository, not by this instance's code.",
      "readmePath": "interaction/README.md",
      "fileCount": 2,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-merge-queue-author-side/folio-assistant/folio-assistant.jsonld#directory/interaction",
      "alternateOf": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/folio-assistant/folio-assistant.jsonld#directory/interaction"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-merge-queue-author-side/folio-assistant/folio-assistant.jsonld#directory/issue-marks",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/ns#Subgraph",
      "name": "issue-marks",
      "path": "issue-marks/",
      "contentSource": {
        "kind": "directory",
        "declaredIn": "default"
      },
      "holdsGraph": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#graphKind/issue-marks"
      ],
      "description": "How far an agent has read an issue: `lastCommentId`, `lastUpdatedAt` and `checkedAt`, one file per issue. NOT the comments — the marks say what was seen, and one of the two files here says so in its own note. Two marks rather than one because a comment EDITED after being read keeps its id, so the id alone would call it seen and an edited requirement is a changed requirement (`issue-working`). `state`: a running process writes one each time it checks. Moved out of `.harness/issue-comments/` on 2026-09-20 for the reason `.beans/` and `.harness/workflow/` moved on 2026-09-18 — the artefacts a person looks for first were the hardest to find. SCOPE IS `repository`, and omitting it was a live defect for an hour on 2026-09-20: without it the path resolves against the INSTANCE, so a consumer looked in `cat-harness/` while the content sat at the repository root — and `harness:dirs` then created the empty instance-level directory to satisfy the declaration, turning declared-but-absent into declared-and-empty, which is the `dh4f` false pass wearing a tidier face. Repository, not instance, for the same reason `beans/` and `todos/` are: these are read by every agent working in this repository, not by this instance's code.",
      "readmePath": "issue-marks/README.md",
      "fileCount": 3,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-merge-queue-author-side/folio-assistant/folio-assistant.jsonld#directory/issue-marks",
      "alternateOf": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/folio-assistant/folio-assistant.jsonld#directory/issue-marks"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-merge-queue-author-side/folio-assistant/folio-assistant.jsonld#directory/root-docs",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/ns#Subgraph",
      "name": "root-docs",
      "path": "docs/",
      "contentSource": {
        "kind": "directory",
        "declaredIn": "default"
      },
      "holdsGraph": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#graphKind/docs"
      ],
      "description": "THE REPOSITORY ROOT'S DOCUMENTATION OVERLAY, managed by this instance. Owner's ruling, 2026-09-21, answering whether the root declares its own docs: \"harness can have docs/ which then get listed under cat-harness/docs/<harness>, there is also docs/ dir in repo root managed by cat-harness. other harness augment or overlay ontop of that (content and behviors)\". SEPARATE FROM THE `docs` ENTRY ABOVE, AND IT HAS TO BE. That one is instance-scoped and `reproduce`, which is what makes a DEPENDENT materialise its own docs/ (bean n0nf slice 1). This one is `scope: \"repository\"`, and a repository-scoped entry is filtered out for dependencies -- cat-harness.ts:3261 and :3507 both skip it unless `link.own`. Re-scoping the existing entry instead of adding this one would therefore have UNDONE slice 1 silently: a dependent would simply stop getting a docs/ and nothing would fail. Two directories answering two questions, so two entries, with distinct ids -- the convention `who-iris-docs` already follows. `dependents` is `skip` for the same reason every other cross-instance repository-scoped entry here is: a dependent never reaches this one at all, and claiming it reproduces would be a promise the resolver does not keep. WHAT MAKES IT NOT `dh4f`: a declared directory that nothing reads is this repository's most-paid-for defect, and an empty overlay is exactly that shape. It is consumed by the site build, which composes it OVER cat-harness/docs/ -- so what it contributes today is nothing VERIFIABLY, pinned by a test asserting an empty overlay produces a byte-identical site, rather than nothing unnoticed.",
      "readmePath": "docs/README.md",
      "fileCount": 2,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-merge-queue-author-side/folio-assistant/folio-assistant.jsonld#directory/root-docs",
      "alternateOf": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/folio-assistant/folio-assistant.jsonld#directory/root-docs"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-merge-queue-author-side/folio-assistant/folio-assistant.jsonld#asset/agent-instructions",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/ns#Asset",
      "name": "agent-instructions",
      "path": "AGENTS.md",
      "assetRole": "agent-instructions",
      "title": "AGENTS.md — folio-assistant",
      "description": "The file every cold agent reads first, and the rules that bind in EVERY layer of this checkout. A layer's own AGENTS.md augments it and never restates it. `source` names the bootstrap instance it descends from, so \"is this still what it was copied from\" is a question that can be ASKED — 'it was copied at init' is not an answer. This provenance sits here rather than on cat-harness's because THIS is the file bootstrap copies at initialisation; cat-harness's own is authored in place and carries no source.",
      "alternateOf": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/folio-assistant/folio-assistant.jsonld#asset/agent-instructions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-merge-queue-author-side/folio-assistant/folio-assistant.jsonld#asset/instance-readme",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/ns#Asset",
      "name": "instance-readme",
      "path": "README.md",
      "assetRole": "instance-readme",
      "title": "folio-assistant",
      "description": "The repository's reader-facing entry point, and the INDEX over every instance in it: its `cat-harness:instances` section is generated from the declarations themselves, giving each instance both an agent entry (AGENTS.md, memories) and a human one (README, docs). Generated sections are written by `readme:sync` only where the file already carries their markers, and `readme:audit` verifies every other link.",
      "alternateOf": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/folio-assistant/folio-assistant.jsonld#asset/instance-readme"
    }
